# Pulse stall reconciler (explore-88k9) — writes the ledger row a DEAD tick could not
# write. A tick that fails before completing its first turn cannot self-report, so its
# fire leaves the ledger silent and the dashboard can only say "stale" — indistinguishable
# from a tick that is merely slow. This watcher runs OUTSIDE the tick (and outside the
# tick-jail), so it survives exactly the conditions that kill one.
#
# Fleet-wide: ONE instance (pair with the .timer), manifest-driven, LLM-free, idempotent
# (the row it appends is itself the "already reconciled" marker). It does NOT re-fire or
# repair anything — writing the truthful row is the whole job.
#
# Inspect: journalctl --user -u pulse-stall.service -n 20
#          cat ~/.local/state/harness/pulse-stall-reconcile.log
[Unit]
Description=Pulse stall reconciler: log a `stalled` row for a fire that never reported

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=%h/.agents/agents/scheduler/pulse-stall-reconcile.py
# Bound the run so a wedged systemctl can never hang the watcher forever.
TimeoutStartSec=180
StandardOutput=append:%h/.local/state/harness/pulse-stall.log
StandardError=append:%h/.local/state/harness/pulse-stall.log
